> [12]: Reading a confused blessed scroll of enchant weapon while
> wielding a +5 quarterstaff in one hand and a dilithium crystal
> in the other [snip grand, elaborate YANI]

So many things wrong with this idea. It's too grand.

* Quarterstaffs are 2-handed. So you can't hold a crystal in the other hand
anyway.
* There is currently only one colour of dilithium crystal. It is also one of
the rarest gems in the game. They don't start appearing in the DoD til level
20 or something.
* Far too special case for such a huge amount of new functionality. You have
to be a wizard or you have to find a staff in bones or wish for one. There's
nothing wrong with class-specific functionality, so long as its simple.
(Priest b/u/cing, Caveman cannibalism, Wizard unknown magic markering)
* What would these coloured dilithium crystals look like un-ided? There are
currently no silver gems in the game.
* What's the point in casting protection only once every few hundred turns?
* (The clincher) What's wrong with wands? Sure, they don't recharge after a
while, but otherwise they're exactly the same as these staves.

